  "novelty": "unknown",
  "construction": "Halving of the gross code [[144,12,12]] (codes/144-12-12.json) along a fixed-point-free ZX-duality that preserves the two blocks (symplectic halving: Lee, Okada, Maskara, Kasai, Zhou, arXiv:2609.30069, Def. 3; Burton, Durso-Sabina, Brown, arXiv:2406.09951, Thm. 3.5). Parent: G = Z/12 x Z/6, element (i,j) with index 6i+j; qubit (1,h) -> index of h, (2,h) -> 72 + index of h; X-check g on (1, g+F_A) and (2, g+F_B), Z-check g on (1, g-F_B) and (2, g-F_A), F_A = {(3,0),(0,1),(0,2)}, F_B = {(0,3),(1,0),(2,0)} (A = x^3+y+y^2, B = y^3+x+x^2; equal to codes/144-12-12.json). Involution: Psi(1,h) = (1, c1 + psi(h)), Psi(2,h) = (2, c2 + psi(h)) with the automorphism psi(1,0) = (3,4), psi(0,1) = (10,3) (psi^2 = 1), c1 = (1,2), c2 = (5,4); it maps the set of X-check supports onto the set of Z-check supports. Fold: Sigma = the parent qubits q with q < Psi(q), in increasing order; fold qubit i is the i-th element sigma_i of Sigma; the X-check a gives the generator with X on {i : sigma_i in a} and Z on {i : Psi(sigma_i) in a}, in the order of the X-checks. n = 72, rank 66, k = 6, all 72 generators of weight 6 without Y; not locally Clifford equivalent to a CSS code.",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "arXiv:2406.09951",
   "arXiv:2308.07915",
   "arXiv:2611.09538",
   "arXiv:2611.08247"
  ],
  "date": "2026-11-10",
  "model": "Claude Opus 5.5",
  "notes": "Distance 9 is exact: no nontrivial logical of Pauli weight <= 8 by four independent exhaustive computations (tropidist b03ec2d4077f in the board's Pauli encoding, certs/72-6-9-s.json in the same pull request; Magma V2.30-1 MinimumDistance; a meet-in-the-middle search over all Paulis of weight <= 4; a search over the logicals with at most four non-Y factors combined with d = 12 of the parent, certs/144-12-12.json), and exactly 24 logicals of weight 9. Programs, data and logs: github.com/TimoKellerMath/quantum-error-correction @ c203901854da, amplified-and-folded-codes/. The CSS entry 72-6-9 has the same parameters; this entry is a non-CSS code for the stabilizer board: the generator-level parity system for single-qubit Cliffords has no solution, and every generator is the only nontrivial stabilizer supported in its support, so no single-qubit Clifford makes the group CSS. It dominates the genon entry 72-6-8-b (same n, k and check weight, d <= 8 by its witness), which is the fold of the same parent along a block-swapping ZX-duality; checked, not equivalent to an existing entry."
